required_approvals.description:
required_approvals is the number of distinct principals whose approval the gate needs (the author and the author's run never count, so it never relaxes
 approver != author). The loader refuses 0, and refuses the field on any gate kind other than GATE_KIND_HUMAN (only a human
 gate counts approvals). Absent means 1. It corresponds to approvers.count of the authority model;
 the count a gate needs is the largest of this value, the policy's approvers.count and any approval floor of a control
 pack, so this field only raises a requirement. Nothing enforces the count yet (a later release owns the rule and an upper bound);
 the loader and the profile context's KeepsGatesOf only preserve it.
